// Regla Sigma: proc_creation_macos_payload_decoded_and_decrypted.yml
// ID Sigma: 234dc5df-40b5-49d1-bf53-0d44ce778eca
// Título: Payload Decoded and Decrypted via Built-in Utilities
// Descripción: Detects when a built-in utility is used to decode and decrypt a payload after a macOS disk image (DMG) is executed. Malware authors may attempt to evade detection and trick users into executing malicious code by encoding and encrypting their payload and placing it in a disk image file. This behavior is consistent with adware or malware families such as Bundlore and Shlayer.
// Aplica a: Producto: macos | Categoría: process_creation
// Producto: macos
// Categoría: process_creation
// Servicio: 
// Nivel: medium
// Pipeline: microsoft_xdr
// Ruta original: C:\SigmaLab\sigma\rules\macos\process_creation\proc_creation_macos_payload_decoded_and_decrypted.yml
// Requiere validación en el entorno de destino.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "/openssl" and (ProcessCommandLine contains "/Volumes/" and ProcessCommandLine contains "enc" and ProcessCommandLine contains "-base64" and ProcessCommandLine contains " -d ")
